/// A program asking polkit for something that needs a password first
/// (`pkexec`, a settings page changing the system): what the dialog
/// shows. `polkit.request` is the one being answered.
record PolkitRequest {
  /// The polkit action asked for (`org.freedesktop.policykit.exec`).
  action_id: text
  /// What polkit says it is for, in your language ("Authentication is
  /// needed to run `/usr/bin/bash' as the super user").
  message: text
  /// The icon the program named for it (a theme icon name), or "".
  icon: text
  /// The user whose password is asked for: you, or an administrator
  /// when the action needs one. Another of `users` is picked with
  /// `polkit.choose(user)`.
  user: text
  /// Every user polkit would take a password from for it (the
  /// administrators, or only you), each once; `user` is one of them.
  users: [text]
  /// What the password check asks ("Password: "), as PAM says it; ""
  /// while it asks nothing (an answer being checked, a fingerprint
  /// reader waiting).
  prompt: text
  /// The answer to `prompt` may be shown as it is typed (PAM asks for
  /// a name, not a secret).
  echo: bool
  /// What PAM last told the user, as it said it ("Place your finger on
  /// the fingerprint reader"), or "".
  info: text
}

/// Strand's own polkit authentication agent: the password dialog when a
/// program asks for something that needs one. While a config reads
/// `polkit`, Strand registers as this session's agent with polkit
/// (unless another agent already is, which it leaves be), and each
/// request polkit sends becomes `request` until it is answered,
/// cancelled, or withdrawn by the program. The password goes to polkit's
/// own helper (`polkit-agent-helper-1`), never checked by Strand, and is
/// wiped once sent. A panel shows it:
/// `panel Polkit { open: polkit.request != null; keyboard: exclusive … }`.
service polkit {
  /// The request being answered, or null when none waits.
  request: PolkitRequest?
  /// How many more requests wait behind `request`, each shown in turn.
  waiting: int
  /// An answer is being checked.
  busy: bool
  /// The last answer was refused: `request` stays, and its prompt asks
  /// again.
  failed: bool
  /// Strand is this session's polkit agent: false while another agent
  /// is (a desktop's own, `polkit-gnome`), or without polkit, when
  /// `error` says why.
  available: bool
  /// Why Strand is not the agent ("another polkit agent serves this
  /// session"), or why the last request could not be answered (no
  /// helper); "" otherwise.
  error: text
  /// Answers `request.prompt` with `answer` (the password), or the next
  /// prompt the check asks: `input { type: password; text: <-> pw; on
  /// activate { polkit.respond(pw); pw = "" } }`. Ignored while one is
  /// being checked.
  action respond(answer: text)
  /// Dismisses `request`: the program is told it was refused, and the
  /// next request, if any, shows.
  action cancel()
  /// Asks for `user`'s password instead (one of `request.users`).
  action choose(user: text)
}
